#: ../../services.rst:58 5d1a07bca5374f2c9b828811c1b63910
#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry:1 d86d0cc5134a433884ecd8751e357419 of
msgid "Retrying SCSI operations that report a transient busy state."
msgstr ""

#: 4c001a7b99664432913d211d58121522 apps.libraries.services.core.retry:3 of
msgid ""
"Moved from tape_operations_service.py:1146 (_execute_mtx_with_retry), the"
" only retry logic in the project and worth keeping: the MHVTL robot "
"reports \"Logical Unit Not Ready\" for a second or two after a move, and "
"a caller that gives up immediately turns a working library into an "
"intermittent one."
msgstr ""

#: 4aafc60bc05f4ea284331f60bd096a6f apps.libraries.services.core.retry:8 of
msgid "Two changes from the original:"
msgstr ""

#: a2e494377ba340f28b62ada4bc6d355b apps.libraries.services.core.retry:10 of
msgid ""
"the delay backs off instead of sleeping a flat 3 seconds five times. The "
"original's worst case was 5 x 30s of command plus 5 x 3s of sleep, which "
"can outlast the gunicorn worker timeout of 120s and kill the request that"
" was waiting for it;"
msgstr ""

#: 96095db2959844c8a4e1550ad9b3a157 apps.libraries.services.core.retry:14 of
msgid ""
"the decision to retry is a named predicate rather than an inline list, so"
" the sense codes can be tested without running mtx."
msgstr ""

#: 85f7cce927b24dbaa0b19ba7459249b8
#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.TRANSIENT_MARKERS:1 of
msgid ""
"Sense text that means \"ask again shortly\" rather than \"this will never"
" work\". ASC=04 is Logical Unit Not Ready; the robot reports it while it "
"finishes a previous move."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.is_transient:1
#: f7c9fe7fa6844cc0a690f4042ed36df8 of
msgid "Is this failure worth retrying?"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.is_transient:3
#: ebee0c30677e4b47a2e7b44b4b2f922c of
msgid ""
"A drive that is genuinely busy with a backup reports \"Device or resource"
" busy\", and so does a robot mid-move; neither is permanent. A bad slot "
"number or a missing device is not transient and retrying only delays the "
"error."
msgstr ""

#: 9596d368a39e45968eed929e11b41f68
#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.retry_on_busy:1 of
msgid "Run an operation, retrying while it reports a transient busy state."
msgstr ""

#: 032e92e716b24a89bddd7c5196c69dc4
#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.retry_on_busy:3 of
msgid "result = retry_on_busy(lambda: shell.sudo(['mtx', '-f', dev, 'status']),"
msgstr ""

#: 821343b0f373491fb3c4c01c6cf15d51
#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.retry_on_busy:4 of
msgid "description='mtx status')"
msgstr ""

#: a68d56a686e34f0d83b4ef3c237b44f2
#: apps.libraries.services.core.retry.retry_on_busy:6 of
msgid ""
"Returns the last result either way, so the caller sees the real error "
"rather than a synthesised one."
msgstr ""

