#: 2b0a702b3d954830813d651ff2699c22
#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.CommandResult.output:1 of
msgid "stdout, or stderr when the command said nothing on stdout."
msgstr ""

#: 8ebc8efd88184dcebdb4c5dca0f2396c apps.libraries.services.core.shell.run:1 of
msgid "Run a command and report what happened."
msgstr ""

#: 6a82b91222af4c55a718b49723421e7e apps.libraries.services.core.shell.run:3 of
msgid ""
"argv is always a list, so there is no shell and nothing in it can be read"
" as a shell metacharacter. A timeout is always set: a wedged mtx call "
"otherwise holds a worker until gunicorn kills it."
msgstr ""

#: 1b4f2e9ae3b547eba2980c68d67f3f3e apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo:1
#: of
msgid "Run a command through sudo."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo:3 bc2d61527f714777ba7b8aad85a7358b
#: of
msgid ""
"Everything MHVTL owns - the config directory, the media directory, the "
"daemons - is root-owned, so mutations go through the sudoers rules "
"shipped in packaging/rpm/mhvtl-gui.sudoers."
msgstr ""

#: 364f8dbf649046cb87fed5564cce6003
#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo_bytes:1 of
msgid "Run a command through sudo and keep its output as bytes."
msgstr ""

#: 5250749ab98d4011b6e29a1ebe4308ae
#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo_bytes:3 of
msgid ""
"run() decodes to text, which is right for every command that prints words"
" and wrong for one that prints a file: replacing undecodable bytes "
"silently corrupts what was read. Returns (ok, stdout bytes, stderr text)."
msgstr ""

#: 512b6799504a4c5db3311cf9f29514fd
#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo_cat:1 of
msgid "Read a possibly root-only file, trying a plain read first."
msgstr ""

#: 9d7e87b6b0834553a05a5cfff4e0ccf0
#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo_cat:3 of
msgid ""
"Most config files are world-readable; library_contents.20 on this host is"
" mode 600. Reading without sudo when possible keeps read-only CLI "
"commands usable by an unprivileged account."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo_tee:1
#: d8faa8577fc84b1e81747300058343f5 of
msgid "Write a root-owned file through tee."
msgstr ""

#: 3cf6c39907b2463c909234a431037f74
#: apps.libraries.services.core.shell.sudo_tee:3 of
msgid ""
"For config files prefer core.locking.atomic_write_text, which locks and "
"renames instead of truncating in place."
msgstr ""

