#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities:3
#: f72d85750d5e4148a750289eefb1b5a9 of
msgid ""
"A library or drive in device.conf is just a vendor string and a product "
"string. The daemons decide from those strings which *personality* to "
"emulate - which inquiry data, which mode pages, and for a library, where "
"in the SCSI element address space its drives, slots, picker and MAP live."
" That last part sets hard limits: a library can only have as many drives "
"as fit between its drive range and the next range, and vtllibrary "
"silently ignores any drive past that point."
msgstr ""

#: 8386649e2cb74a86871c639756fc47b4
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities:10 of
msgid ""
"This module is a transcription of those decisions, with a reference to "
"the line in MHVTL that each one comes from, so that the web UI and the "
"CLI can say before writing device.conf what MHVTL will do with it. It is "
"checked against the MHVTL source by tests/test_personalities.py whenever "
"the source tree is present."
msgstr ""

#: 5335e49916014bf4b195ae3771cdbe97
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities:15 of
