"(field, prefix, then-function or sub-selector). Matching is case-"
"insensitive over the prefix's length - strncasecmp - against the vendor "
"or product as read from device.conf. usr/cmd/vtllibrary.c:1461 "
"customise_lu and the customise_*_lu functions at 1421 (IBM), 1430 (STK), "
"1443 (HP) and 1450 (Spectra)."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.LIBRARY_SELECTOR:7
#: d136442680fb470b93ee99b71ac2b384 of
msgid ""
"Worth knowing: ADIC, QUANTUM and OVERLAND are matched on the *product*, "
"not the vendor. Upstream changed this in 24f7342 (\"library: Fix vendor "
"'QUANTUM' not 'SCALAR'\", for issue #152, where a product of \"Scalar "
"i2000\" misbehaved under the Scalar personality). So vendor QUANTUM with "
"product \"Scalar i500\" - what a real Quantum library reports - gets the "
"default layout, and the Scalar layout is reached only by a product "
"beginning \"ADIC\" or \"QUANTUM\"."
msgstr ""

#: 43393e88695947d1b3fe23dea158ed8b
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.LIBRARY_SELECTOR:14 of
msgid "vtllibrary's selector, in order"
msgstr ""

#: 8c65fb821e614d03b8c6fa8cb59495b9
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.SCALAR_PRODUCT_PREFIXES:1 of
msgid "1470-1473)."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.SCALAR_PRODUCT_PREFIXES:3
#: fe4b34e5ac604aa1a1b20aff59f04daf of
msgid "The product prefixes that select init_scalar_smc (vtllibrary.c"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.scalar_layout_product:1
#: f6393554fd7c486a98f3def152de206e of
msgid "A product string that gets the Scalar layout, for a Scalar model."
msgstr ""

#: 6963f3438b09474baac8449d8f1e595c
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.scalar_layout_product:3 of
msgid ""
"MHVTL gives init_scalar_smc only to a product beginning ADIC or QUANTUM, "
"which no real Scalar reports (\"Scalar i2000\"), so a profile model never"
" reaches it. The variant puts the vendor in front of the model - dropping"
" the word \"Scalar\" when that is needed to fit the 16-character product "
"field - and returns None for a vendor that is not one of the two or a "
"model that is not a Scalar."
msgstr ""

#: 3c035d909d4d4fdfa3c6a3c9796ce529
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.scalar_layout_product:10 of
msgid ""
"ADIC,    Scalar 1000   ->  \"ADIC Scalar 1000\" ADIC,    Scalar i2000  ->"
"  \"ADIC i2000\" QUANTUM, Scalar i500   ->  \"QUANTUM i500\""
msgstr ""

#: 87fe6aa609744ad2ad574460879dca52
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.library_layout:1 of
msgid "The layout vtllibrary will use for this vendor and product."
msgstr ""

#: 93ff0c4027d344a89456f430b86aa67c
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.DRIVE_PERSONALITIES:1 of
msgid ""
"132 (tape_drives[]), matched by config_lu() at usr/cmd/vtltape.c:1899 "
"(local; upstream 1885): an exact, case-sensitive comparison of the "
"product padded to 16 characters. A product not in this table is emulated "
"as a generic drive (init_default_ssc), which backup software will not "
"recognise as the model it was told to expect."
msgstr ""

#: 6facd0d776b24d7788da59751d5ca0b1
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.DRIVE_PERSONALITIES:7 of
msgid "vtltape's table, usr/cmd/vtltape.c"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.drive_personality:1
#: f770630b5a7c47d7bff26b1fc8d773c3 of
msgid "The personality vtltape will emulate for this product string."
msgstr ""

#: 2cf4787cfc6b41cfbe5bea42b5e14e3e
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.MediaSupport:1 of
msgid "The cartridges a drive personality loads, and whether it can write them."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.MediaSupport:3
#: dfe5f9795e4341a5a4b35061e2831504 of
msgid ""
"Transcribed from add_drive_media_list(lu, LOAD_RW | LOAD_RO, ...) in each"
" init_* function, and for LTO-7 and later from the tdN_media tables. What"
" a drive does not list, it refuses: vtltape unloads the cartridge again "
"(usr/cmd/vtltape.c:1512, \"Load failed: Data format not suitable\") and "
"leaves it in the drive for someone to unmount."
msgstr ""

#: 7bf5f6de9fd1442a80be84f606fa5543
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.MediaSupport.loads:1 of
msgid "Everything the drive accepts, native first."
msgstr ""

#: 88b1865bf0ff467da88c9288bd835419
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.DRIVE_MEDIA:1 of
msgid ""
"Drive personality -> what it loads. Cleaning and WORM entries are left "
"out: a WORM cartridge is the same density made with mktape -t WORM."
msgstr ""

#: 47b0de70adfa427cb2976c8686ba8a92
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.SUFFIX_BY_DENSITY:1 of
msgid ""
"Density -> the two-character barcode suffix a data cartridge carries, as "
"make_vtl_media reads it back (usr/cmd/make_vtl_media.in:81-168, upstream "
"81-164) and etc/generate_library_contents.in:66-90 documents it. A "
"density with no suffix here cannot be named by a barcode, so it cannot be"
" created: DLT3 and SDLT1 exist only as read-only legacy media."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.SUFFIX_BY_DENSITY:7
#: d4555baf7444475780d2bfeea46b7b0d of
msgid ""
"Upstream make_vtl_media cannot read three of these back: its suffix "
"pattern (make_vtl_media.in:91 upstream) has no C or T in the second "
"position, so TC (T10KC) and LT (LTO-3 WORM) come out UNKNOWN, and it has "
"no branch for JC (E06), though the legend documents it. The local tree "
"carries the fix (patches/1.8-upstream-submission/0006). This app passes "
"the density to mktape itself, so all three work here either way; an "
"unpatched hand-run make_vtl_media stops at the first such tape. "
"tests/test_media checks both."
msgstr ""

#: 0e9ea23d9c8a44beaa5493532891deba
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.DENSITY_BY_SUFFIX:1 of
msgid ""
"Suffix -> density, including the WORM suffixes, which name the same "
"density as the data cartridge. The 3592 WORM suffixes follow "
"make_vtl_media (JW and JX -> E05, JY -> E07), not the comment beside "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.NATIVE_CAPACITY_GB:1
#: cb892caf666e4c168d4e29ecee222c16 of
msgid ""
"Density -> native capacity in GB (SI), from media_native_capacity() "
"(usr/vtllib.c:1700). mktape -s 0 creates a tape of exactly this size. The"
" 9840 and 9940 media are not in that switch and fall to its 1 GB default,"
" so they are left out here and a size should always be given for them."
msgstr ""

#: 609402eb90634101a166217af1deb4a7
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.media_label:1 of
msgid "'LTO8 (12 TB)', for a drop-down."
msgstr ""

#: 0ecb9e8dc76141219b487b68583c5938
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.WORM_SUFFIX_BY_DENSITY:1 of
msgid "69-74)."
msgstr ""

#: 824ce7fd7469405c8dd5dbc78c7077ff
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.WORM_SUFFIX_BY_DENSITY:3 of
msgid ""
"LTO density -> the suffix of its WORM cartridge "
"(generate_library_contents.in"
msgstr ""

#: 977e8bcfd5364ea1a68b5995ba367c64
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.suffix_for:1 of
msgid "The barcode suffix for a density: the WORM one for a WORM LTO tape."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.drive_media:1
#: c712c2eb0fde4449b85947cf37b8dfe0 of
msgid ""
"What a drive with this product string loads, or None for the generic "
"personality, which MHVTL gives no media list at all."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.creatable_media:1
#: da8415b2affa48198178c3a9ec477434 of
msgid "The media a library with this drive can be filled with."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.creatable_media:3
#: c76091839247483a8451f7322f4d4f3a of
msgid ""
"Everything the drive loads that a barcode can name, native first. The "
"read-only generation is included - a restore library is a real thing to "
"build - and validation warns about it."
msgstr ""

#: 5244da1e1b8a4221954ace7f425a95ca
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.read_only_media:1 of
msgid "The media this drive loads but cannot write."
msgstr ""

#: ac4ee64ce4b046ab9f38aff2ecdff058
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.density_for_barcode:1 of
msgid "The density a barcode's last two characters declare, or None."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.media_verdict:1
#: f4990312a9e44db09962ba84745df544 of
msgid "Whether a drive with this product string loads this density, and how."
msgstr ""

#: 33d5fd0b841e4affa0a348a787535ddf
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.media_verdict:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{'known': bool, 'can_read': bool, 'can_write': bool}. known is False when"
" either side is unrecognised: MHVTL decides on load, and the caller "
"should say so rather than refuse."
msgstr ""

#: 36036b8ab30748afac7bb8f14f8d8cbc
#: apps.libraries.services.profiles.personalities.limits_problems:1 of
msgid "Everything about these counts that MHVTL would silently not emulate."
msgstr ""

