msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:158 0e2c0c6c5e524061822164b2fe144427
msgid "Library lifecycle: list, create, update, delete, orphans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:161 51f69d3d530b4fb5b5ae6107bfd60cde
msgid "``lifecycle``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:163 4472e00c97ed49a5970aa582f6ba93db
#: 671a30380093417d93f3e7af42354c37
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:1 of
msgid "Creating and deleting a library: the paths that write device.conf."
msgstr ""

#: 50bfbec84ec5462b968fccae41022605
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:3 of
msgid ""
"Moved from mhvtl_library_service.py:create_library (171 lines) and "
"delete_library (93), with the helpers they called. These two change the "
"configuration every daemon reads, so what they do is worth stating "
"plainly."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:7
#: ea295e85a4664039b29e1a724cf5a9aa of
msgid "Creating a library, in order:"
msgstr ""

#: 1fa54b3ca0a24ef7afc6000892cb66ae
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:9 of
msgid "fill in what the vendor profile decides      spec.apply_defaults"
msgstr ""

#: 0fefe80721f24f049e8dcb86ccb947f1
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:10 of
msgid "validate the finished specification          validation.validate"
msgstr ""

#: 19c29ae9252c4234a6316fe1db32ff1c
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:11 of
msgid "back up the configuration                    config.ConfigService.backup"
msgstr ""

#: 71417448d1194bbbb47f5fcce84b4541
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:12 of
msgid "write device.conf                            config.device_conf"
msgstr ""

#: 7b4347c405a040bcaac883534ee3e7d9
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:13 of
msgid "write library_contents.<id>                  config.library_contents"
msgstr ""

#: 651e95ac7e6947e8a57204d382d1b143
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:14 of
msgid "enable and start the systemd units           console.units"
msgstr ""

#: 817f35fa75594237bddefba0a2db9d8e
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:16 of
msgid ""
"Deleting reverses it: stop the units first, then remove the configuration"
" they read. A daemon whose device.conf entry has vanished logs errors "
"until it is killed, and a library_contents file removed under a running "
"robot is worse."
msgstr ""

#: 103a56735c2c40e5be40f61c4deb52a1
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:20 of
msgid "Two rules hold throughout:"
msgstr ""

#: a2730f44ca72482399e97bbe6fba86fc
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:22 of
msgid ""
"The backup is taken before anything is written, and the write is refused "
"if the backup fails. The alternative is a half-written device.conf and no"
" copy of what was there before - which is how 72 tapes were lost once "
"already."
msgstr ""

#: 77267540d3cb4e7db4ad4de028bc1bf0
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:26 of
msgid ""
"Any failure after the first write restores the backup. A create that "
"fails between device.conf and library_contents leaves a library the "
"daemons will start and the robot cannot use."
msgstr ""

#: 0a4ed1d2e2214c94ae535b7c2e388282
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle:30 of
msgid ""
"One duplication removed on the way. create_library repeated three profile"
" compatibility checks inline - media supported by the library, drive "
"compatible with the library, media supported by the drive - and then "
"called validate_library, which checks the same three and more. The inline"
" copies are gone; validation.validate is the complete version."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.daemons_are_ours:1
#: c9c1403bdc8d4d9984837fcfe057d4c2 of
msgid "Do the running daemons read this configuration directory?"
msgstr ""

#: 2007d0b1788b4d8fbbb62231e58f58f5
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.daemons_are_ours:3 of
msgid ""
"They read the live one. An operation writing somewhere else - a test, a "
"scratch copy, a restore staged elsewhere - must not start or stop them: "
"it would apply a file they never read, and stop libraries that are in "
"use."
msgstr ""

#: 36f98520425546c2a6f9a7ec55e536d3
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.allocate_targets:1 of
msgid "One SCSI target for the library, then one per drive."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.allocate_targets:3
#: d081f7f3a07247589114749efd766ffb of
msgid ""
"Contiguous above the highest target in use when that fits under "
"MAX_TARGET, otherwise the first free run, otherwise any free targets - "
"config/ids.targets says why in each case. Raises ids.OutOfIds when fewer "
"are free than needed."
msgstr ""

#: 1895abf24b764fb580c51603c3105c0a 6905e9e2707c4cbfb82d0260cb37addf
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create:1
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.service.LibraryService.create:1 of
msgid "Create a library, its drives and its media slots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst 54f3fce149fe458ba64aeb88b1658213
#: 6d4dacdc096544e58bebe6fc1adf2628 7ab45bcf420d43109ec974bf065e98de
#: afed1aa304144f9ebeccca291517ef3b
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create
#: da3a49b5e5f34d0594e130d5841f357f of
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: 21d0d60fd09143c4b5e6830d3966de9b
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create:3 of
msgid ""
"at minimum a profile key; see spec.apply_defaults for what is filled in "
"and what may be overridden."
msgstr ""

#: 26bad89e4460490da54900ef58c2f7e9
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create:5 of
msgid ""
"which /etc/mhvtl to write. Always passed explicitly by tests - a service "
"that defaults to the live directory once created a library on the running"
" host."
msgstr ""

#: a254b0f99c134724bdf465db6d82b965
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create:8 of
msgid "called to allocate an id when the specification has none."
msgstr ""

#: 1fa751b14b8f413a833a05b4d730041d
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create:9 of
msgid ""
"enable and start the units. False leaves the configuration written and "
"the daemons down, which is what an operator creating several libraries at"
" once wants."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.create:13
#: eede33f7c4424aaaa60bf052792303b5 of
msgid ""
"Returns a failure, not an exception, for anything an operator can fix: an"
" unknown profile, an id already in use, media the drive cannot read."
msgstr ""

#: 9af2f7832583452ea35f56ad0b99bdb2
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.preview:1 of
msgid "The device.conf text create() would append, without writing anything."
msgstr ""

#: 990101bc7e4345dc914b382211319ba5
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.preview:3 of
msgid ""
"The same defaults, validation and id and target planning as create(), so "
"the create form shows the ids and addresses the library would really get."
" The adapter this replaces allocated targets but not drive ids, so its "
"preview could show drive ids create() would not use."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.preview:8
#: b7208ea8ead046b1802b339fb963dbc8 of
msgid ""
"Validation problems do not stop the preview: they are returned beside the"
" text, because the form shows both. Errors and warnings stay apart - an "
"error is what create() would refuse, a warning is what it would accept "
"and grumble about - and a caller that wants them together can add the two"
" lists."
msgstr ""

#: 3db2bc11a3d64212ba972918e0726867
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.check_safe_to_delete:1 of
msgid "Is anything loaded in this library's drives?"
msgstr ""

#: 1d3c76b46dd34da7b4d9ea29475602bd
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.check_safe_to_delete:3 of
msgid ""
"Deleting a library with a tape in a drive loses whatever the drive has "
"not yet flushed, and leaves a media file that no library claims. An "
"offline library is safe - there is nothing running to lose - so a status "
"call that fails is not by itself a refusal: it usually means the daemons "
"are down, which is the state a delete is heading for anyway."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.delete:1
#: e5694d2df8eb408e99e87eef1e91e40d of
msgid "Remove a library, its drives, its contents file and optionally its media."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.delete:3
#: d360bfb24b5748b996a29b54a05cbf17 of
msgid ""
"Media is kept unless asked for: the tapes under a library's barcodes are "
"data, and a library definition is cheap to recreate. force skips the "
"loaded-tape check, which is the operator saying they know."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.update:1
#: d691a804623b4210aae08e8aa2bcf60c of
msgid "Change a library, by deleting it and creating it again."
msgstr ""

#: 460f1f572a4048aab7e9d86c92cc6c41
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.update:3 of
msgid ""
"Moved from mhvtl_library_service.py:update_library. MHVTL has no way to "
"change a library in place - vendor, product and drive count are all read "
"once at daemon start - so an update is a delete followed by a create, "
"under one lock, with one backup around both."
msgstr ""

#: 781569be6b494c6394bc5470d57d194d
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.update:8 of
msgid ""
"What that costs the operator, stated because the old version did not: "
"library_contents is regenerated, so slot assignments and any hand-edited "
"barcodes are replaced by a fresh series. Media files are kept, but a tape"
" whose barcode is no longer in the new series is no longer in the "
"library."
msgstr ""

#: 211d31faea044fe497d942437dfeb8aa
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.update:13 of
msgid ""
"force is not offered. An update that stops the daemons while a tape is "
"loaded is the case the loaded-drive check exists for, and an operator who"
" means it can delete with force and create."
msgstr ""

#: 468adb76155b4dc4b490a6779a84dd2c
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.recognised:1 of
msgid "Has the running system actually picked this library up?"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.recognised:3
#: e557c58bb64a49759a69c14cab03d2d1 of
msgid ""
"Three things have to agree: device.conf declares it, its contents file "
"exists, and its robot daemon is active. Any one of them alone is the "
"state after a half-finished create."
msgstr ""

#: 1ec930ff343a41899d1678af751ad3d1
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.set_empty_slots:1 of
msgid "Change how many empty slots a library has, keeping its tapes."
msgstr ""

#: 67986ac438f44770ad948f7347c7f8b8
#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.set_empty_slots:3 of
msgid ""
"Slots live in library_contents, which the vtllibrary daemon reads once at"
" start, so this rewrites the file and the caller restarts the library - "
"nothing here touches device.conf or any media. The tapes stay in the slot"
" numbers they are in: renumbering them would move a tape the robot has "
"already reported at a given address."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.libraries.lifecycle.set_empty_slots:9
#: bedc0e6f9d0a4549bb3c88987ca92382 of
msgid ""
"Growing appends empty slots after the last one. Shrinking removes empty "
"slots from the end and stops at the first tape, because MHVTL stops "
"reading at the first missing slot number - a gap would silently shorten "
"the library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:171 ../../services.rst:236 ../../services.rst:291
