msgid ""
"device.conf parsing and writing go through services/config, which owns "
"the file format; this module only decides what a drive record should "
"contain."
msgstr ""

#: 0c26b2206096461daae353497ad7c841
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DEFAULT_VENDOR:1 of
msgid "Defaults for a new drive, matching what MHVTL's own generator writes."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService:1
#: be96e6ecd92d4e5383ed34a2ac59d28a of
msgid "Drives, as described by device.conf."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService:3
#: d50b967a852e49fdb7aef3ec94f598a6 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"DriveService().list(library_id=10) DriveService().add(10, {'vendor': "
"'IBM', 'product': 'ULT3580-TD8'})"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.list:1
#: fd49b90fa8604fe9bc0b75d312e911c5 of
msgid "Every drive, or just one library's drives."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.get:1
#: c21efa5972fd40ea862dba302bc0111b of
msgid "One drive by its queue id."
msgstr ""

#: 1e9dfe1933454d8789002a130b6801e3
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.activity:1 of
msgid "What each of a library's drives is doing, live and already worded."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.activity:3
#: f63c141d39a241218acb7d96382d9a4b of
msgid ""
"The counters come from `vtlcmd <drive> stats`, which asks the daemon over"
" its message queue and so answers while a backup is running - mt and mtx "
"cannot, because the kernel holds the SCSI reservation for the initiator. "
"That command is our own addition to MHVTL (patches/0004)."
msgstr ""

#: 16277204313d4feda3a4bec408d43568
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.activity:8 of
msgid ""
"MHVTL reports totals, not a rate, so \"writing\" is two readings with a "
"larger number in the second. Which is why the deciding happens here "
"rather than in the page: `mhvtl status activity` has to reach the same "
"answer, and a browser is not the only thing that asks."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.activity:13
#: c184b0b6b6c140269558812c04859b45 of
msgid ""
"The last reading of each drive is kept, so a caller that asks again "
"within _SAMPLE_LIFE seconds gets its comparison for free. A caller with "
"nothing to compare against - a command run once - waits `settle` seconds "
"and reads a second time. Pass settle=0 to refuse that wait and get "
"\"holding\" instead of \"writing\"."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.activity:19
#: bb2d2d9e7112448f934f306848454925 of
msgid "Every drive gets a row, tape or no tape."
msgstr ""

#: 8e5ab689a76742e1a7e62b527d73dfd0
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.placement:1 of
msgid "Where the next drive would land, and which models this library takes."
msgstr ""

#: 8a56701b391e46c7abb57d952059e9bc
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.placement:3 of
msgid ""
"What add() would do, without doing it: the slot, the drive id, the SCSI "
"target and the serial it would be given, the drives the library's profile"
" allows, and whether there is room for another at all. The page shows "
"this before the operator commits, and add() computes it the same way, so "
"the two cannot disagree."
msgstr ""

#: 7417baa1646c407f8c3ad28996a7fe16
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.add:1 of
msgid "Add a drive to an existing library."
msgstr ""

#: 8a9a5173a7e64ef28528235240bf6855
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.add:3 of
msgid ""
"The drive id comes from config/ids: library_id + slot while that is free "
"and not a multiple of ten, otherwise the next free id - MHVTL ties a "
"drive to its library by the Library ID line, not by the id. This used to "
"take library_id + slot unconditionally and check it only against other "
"drives, so a tenth drive on library 10 got id 20, library 20's id."
msgstr ""

#: 176beb2ae60a475bb356cc098356d909
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.add:9 of
msgid ""
"The SCSI target is the lowest free one: device.conf addresses need not be"
" contiguous, and reusing a taken target would give two devices the same "
"address."
msgstr ""

#: 90b7eb4134b149cfa172e8b2b7cad7f1
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.add:13 of
msgid ""
"The drive model defaults to the model the library's drives already are, "
"and the count is checked against the element layout of the library model "
"MHVTL emulates (profiles/personalities), because MHVTL ignores a drive "
"past that limit rather than reporting it."
msgstr ""

#: 1df9887174574c8ea145d333de48c3c4
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.remove:1 of
msgid "Remove a drive from device.conf and from its library_contents."
msgstr ""

#: 0f6f394b39bf4ecc8efc76807fe4942d
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.update:1 of
msgid "Change a drive's vendor, product or serial."
msgstr ""

#: 474b9507651047af9f9150fa6503104e
#: apps.libraries.services.drives.service.DriveService.update:3 of
msgid ""
"Only the identification fields: changing a drive's SCSI address or its "
"library means removing it and adding it again, because both affect the id"
" and the device mapping."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:256 adbfa1e723c54afd82d194b7d74e823c
msgid "``services.tapes``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:258 f5ebb6f46286451e9e9ef19d7c774541
msgid "Tape media: barcodes, densities, and the files under the media directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:261 8ab3a2efa9d742189b498e49833aa6b9
msgid "``barcodes``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:263 7d3cf251e56a47d79a6c5a3708a67b9f
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes:1 d033d9435a5842a3b6dbda1cba58e0b0 of
msgid "Barcodes, prefixes and media densities."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes:3 f9c67958037945d0b77fe0a152438b92 of
msgid ""
"Gathers what was scattered across tape_operations_service.py:244 "
"(get_density_suffix_mapping), :290 (get_lto_from_barcode), :1603 "
"(get_existing_barcodes), the prefix detection at :1539, and the eleven-"
"line prefix block duplicated verbatim in tape_operations_views.py:747-760"
" and :852-865."
msgstr ""

#: 6dbc4b10a26443ea88f18926d9350acb apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes:9 of
msgid ""
"Validation lives here because of where a barcode ends up. It is "
"interpolated into `sudo mktape -m <barcode>` and into `sudo rm -rf "
"<media>/<barcode>`, and the only check before this was `len(barcode) >= "
"4`. A barcode of '../..' was a working path traversal into a root-owned "
"delete. One rule, one place:"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes:14 eacb1179fb6f4bc190f75de52237f9d0
#: of
#, python-brace-format
msgid "VALID_BARCODE = ^[A-Z0-9]{1,16}$"
msgstr ""

#: 524d1b937d4a4cfeabc6bd508493b46f apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes:16
#: of
msgid ""
"That is the SMC physical cartridge label charset, and mktape refuses more"
" than 16 characters anyway."
msgstr ""

#: 45e3c331ab3a49d9aeeb56325921edf0
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.BARCODE_RE:1 of
msgid ""
"The only shape a barcode may take. Checked before the value reaches any "
"command line or path."
msgstr ""

#: 73ac3c2e2434497ca577e794dd5aa227
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.CLEANING_PREFIX:1 of
msgid "Leading characters MHVTL reads as a media kind rather than as data."
msgstr ""

#: ae27568d2fb849f59254c6ce89d9eb35
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.PREFIX_LENGTH:1 of
msgid "How many characters of a barcode are the library's prefix."
msgstr ""

#: 70a516f35d654a428efe3bd329379047
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.InvalidBarcode:1 of
msgid "The barcode is not a shape we are willing to put on a command line."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.validate:1
#: f5c7905482334590a7eba71b94e7db59 of
msgid "Return the barcode, or raise InvalidBarcode saying why it was refused."
msgstr ""

#: 6cd73222d5014487866ea5823784be2b
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.kind:1 of
msgid "data, clean or WORM, as MHVTL reads the leading characters."
msgstr ""

#: 0730e318b82c4fad9fc11544c415ca11
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.density_for:1 of
msgid "Density from the two-character suffix, or None if it is not one we know."
msgstr ""

#: 49640319d6f54806952d02cc33e4dd11
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.GENERATION_CLASS:1 of
msgid ""
"Which palette entry a generation is drawn with. css/mhvtl-console.css "
"defines five, built from the theme's own tokens; anything older or "
"unrecognised shares the last one."
msgstr ""

#: 5f94c463ee17444e878f276a269644db
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.generation_class:1 of
msgid "The CSS class for a density: LTO8 -> 'lto-8'."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.generation_class:3
#: d1dace677c2545c78c8dcacac88d3edc of
msgid ""
"The mount page worked this out in JavaScript, which meant the rule lived "
"in a browser and the tape tiles would have needed their own copy of it."
msgstr ""

#: 8ea672e30f5f4fd8aa246f94bd398eef
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.suffix_for:1 of
msgid "The barcode suffix a density is written with."
msgstr ""

#: 8b6fc0415e5242be8711f09291872379
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.split:1 of
msgid "(prefix, number, suffix) - E01001L8 becomes ('E01', '001', 'L8')."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.build:1
#: d4752046c22a4150af485853ffa60d21 of
msgid "Assemble a barcode and check it before returning it."
msgstr ""

#: 65e9ed10ece24f719d9eed2c200f9706
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.detect_prefix:1 of
msgid "The prefix a library is actually using."
msgstr ""

#: 5097438b4f754d509ad3b70a3f64e4fc
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.detect_prefix:3 of
msgid ""
"Read from the data tapes already in the library rather than computed from"
" a brand table: a library whose database record disagrees with its media "
"would otherwise get barcodes that do not match the ones already in its "
"slots. Cleaning and WORM cartridges are skipped because their prefixes "
"are fixed."
msgstr ""

#: 413e9528bba7499e85b2c81d292ed548
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.detect_suffix:1 of
msgid "The media suffix a library is actually using."
msgstr ""

#: 53cc969c08ad44e28b4b1bbdaaabb424
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.used_numbers:1 of
msgid "The numbers already taken under a prefix."
msgstr ""

#: 7b4fc34874524d5b8e651dea507633dc
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.used_numbers:3 of
msgid ""
"The suffix is not part of the match by default, because the number space "
"is shared across tape generations: a library that already holds E01001L7 "
"must not hand out E01001L8, which would be a second tape with the same "
"number in the same library and an operator reading barcodes off a shelf "
"cannot tell them apart. Pass a suffix only to ask about one generation "
"specifically."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.next_number:1
#: dd7d8999e1e14758a5be45baee09aa84 of
msgid "The first unused number in a series, filling gaps before extending it."
msgstr ""

#: 2fba52fd13e743d4966f299bd3987a48
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.next_number:3 of
msgid ""
"Filling gaps matters: a library that has had tapes deleted would "
"otherwise keep counting upwards and leave holes no operator asked for."
msgstr ""

#: 26c53097d31042ebaf79f84512021717
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.consecutive_free:1 of
msgid "How many numbers are free in a row from `start`."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.consecutive_free:3
#: b4a31e76787f4e1195e7de371ce58420 of
msgid ""
"What a bulk-create form needs to know before offering to make N tapes. "
"Capped at `limit`, and the cap is reported as the number itself: 999 "
"means \"999 or more\", which is enough for any real library."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.series:1
#: fbd96bf583314743910601cc94c5a167 of
msgid "A run of consecutive barcodes, validated before any of them is used."
msgstr ""

#: 32034599f6924e328669b4763f6f73d6
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.KIND_DIGITS:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The number field of each kind of cartridge, and so how many a library can"
" hold: data {prefix}{nnn}, cleaning CLN{lib}{n}, WORM W{brand}{lib}{nn}. "
"The formats are the ones the original bulk-create used and the create "
"pages still preview; the step 8 port had dropped them, so a \"cleaning\" "
"run was made with data barcodes, which MHVTL does not treat as cleaning "
"cartridges."
msgstr ""

#: 2fb61d7f16a44c1e8bf112f6c1c43c4c
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.kind_head:1 of
msgid "Everything before the number, for a kind of cartridge."
msgstr ""

#: 54a7a2bfc8e8462d96f03552c0a8d289
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.kind_head:3 of
msgid ""
"data    E01            E01001L8   (prefix is the library's data prefix) "
"clean   CLN10          CLN101L8 WORM    WE10           WE1001LY   "
"(prefix's first letter is the brand)"
msgstr ""

#: 358fef4ecba34448b41052d46a9eb23e
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.numbers_under:1 of
msgid "The numbers taken after `head`, whatever the suffix."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.barcodes.first_free:1
#: e86894fae24a45ed9e2d2a99b56d39f2 of
msgid "The first unused number after `head`, filling gaps first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:271 de5ffd4bf9eb41da8aa455df7dfb369d
msgid "``compatibility``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:273 34bb8a37498b4779809018e162a596d1
#: 765ff7c6249846e692b1aa7a58b77b43
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:1 of
msgid "Can this cartridge go in that drive?"
msgstr ""

#: 5e3455c1600041bc9e143481a58a75e7
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:3 of
msgid ""
"Moved from tape_operations_service.py (LTO_COMPATIBILITY, "
"DRIVE_MODEL_TO_LTO, BARCODE_SUFFIX_TO_LTO, get_lto_from_barcode, "
"check_tape_drive_compatibility)."
msgstr ""

#: 9d83139603a141e2bea284cc453472ec
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:6 of
msgid ""
"The LTO rule, as MHVTL 1.8 emulates it - and it is not the one-rule-fits-"
"all \"reads two back, writes one back\" this module used to state:"
msgstr ""

#: a296535ed86d42018b52551b55ec55ed
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:9 of
msgid ""
"LTO-1         reads and writes LTO-1 LTO-2         reads and writes LTO-2"
" and LTO-1 LTO-3 .. 7    reads and writes n and n-1; reads n-2 LTO-8"
"         reads and writes LTO-8 and LTO-7 only LTO-9         reads and "
"writes LTO-9 and LTO-8 only LTO-10        reads and writes LTO-10 (and "
"LTO-10 Premium) only"
msgstr ""

#: 2b0f56b1ee5a40d5a7b72ca8b0a7d587
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:16 of
msgid ""
"The table used to have LTO-8 reading LTO-6 and LTO-9 reading LTO-7, so "
"the operator page offered mounts MHVTL refuses. Transcribed from the "
"drive personalities in usr/pm/ult3580_pm.c and usr/pm/hp_ultrium_pm.c, "
"and checked against them by tests/test_personalities."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:21
#: b99c6bfd09044f9e8f88e3a292106d4f of
msgid ""
"Two generations of the same number are not always the same cartridge. A "
"WORM cartridge carries a different suffix (LU is LTO-4 WORM) but the same"
" generation for compatibility, because the drive's read and write "
"capability does not change - what changes is whether the medium can be "
"overwritten, which is the tape's property and not the drive's."
msgstr ""

#: 76b35b43f26748648a11d6050a84f688
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:27 of
msgid ""
"The LTO table is the one with generation-aware messages (\"too new\", "
"\"too old\"). verdict() is what callers use: it answers for any cartridge"
" and any drive, LTO or not, from profiles/personalities.DRIVE_MEDIA, and "
"falls back to \"cannot tell\" - never to a refusal - when the barcode or "
"the product string is one MHVTL's tables do not name."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility:33
#: d39be48b8b704269a57ba07849611176 of
msgid ""
"Why the table is not in profiles/: profiles answer \"what may an operator"
" configure\", from vendor tables. This answers \"what will the hardware "
"do with what is already in the slots\", which is asked of libraries that "
"were configured elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: 894a16b7c04b4b5980b91ae7c8da8388
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.LTO_COMPATIBILITY:1 of
msgid "drive generation -> what it can read, and what it can write."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.DRIVE_MODEL_TO_LTO:1
#: ea4f8faccb234abc85b6193974919bec of
msgid ""
"The product identification string a drive reports, by generation. This is"
" what device.conf carries and what SCSI inquiry returns, so it is how a "
"drive is recognised without asking the daemon anything."
msgstr ""

#: 42a774bab9e44e5fa7684f5678289680
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.BARCODE_SUFFIX_TO_LTO:1 of
msgid ""
"The two-character barcode suffix, by generation. The W* entries are WORM "
"cartridges: same generation for read and write capability, different "
"medium."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.lto_for_barcode:1
#: f4fb549d050940b5a58e5b4c1eb44298 of
msgid "The LTO generation a barcode's suffix declares, or None."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.lto_for_barcode:3
#: d2b6fbeb4c5945f19e023fc1e4e21963 of
msgid ""
"None for a cartridge that is not LTO at all - a T10000 or 3592 barcode is"
" perfectly valid and simply has no LTO generation. Callers show "
"\"unknown\" rather than refusing the tape."
msgstr ""

#: 084d003fb3b947ee9a61644b74abe6f5
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.lto_for_drive_model:1 of
msgid "The LTO generation a drive's product identification declares, or None."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.check:1
#: c807de318e0a4d108d04ddcd18b52530 of
msgid "Whether a cartridge can be read and written in a drive."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.check:3
#: ec1ec275a4394015ad2a09d2c675f190 of
msgid ""
"Returns compatible/can_read/can_write and a message written for an "
"operator: \"too new for\" and \"too old for\" are the two ways this "
"fails, and they need different actions, so the message says which."
msgstr ""

#: 24fa95ccf525426d87890a08bdb16844
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.drives_for_tape:1 of
msgid "Which of these drives could take this cartridge."
msgstr ""

#: 79eb9fd2bae04efbb54e2fce83c5c25b
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.drives_for_tape:3 of
msgid ""
"Each drive is a dict with at least lto_generation and drive_num; only "
"drives with nothing loaded are offered, because a mount into a full drive"
" fails whatever the generations are."
msgstr ""

#: 9e098f76f08041e4ad188221ca7b85ce
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.verdict:1 of
msgid "Can the cartridge with this barcode go into a drive with this product?"
msgstr ""

#: 41108c68cc1e45dcab7258db70b0d083
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.verdict:3 of
msgid ""
"The one question the mount page, the mount service and the CLI all ask. "
"Returns known/compatible/can_read/can_write/message, plus what was "
"recognised (tape_density, tape_lto, drive_lto) so a page can show it."
msgstr ""

#: 28119741d9684eda8fd3258a0bfc7c0d
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.verdict:7 of
msgid ""
"compatible is False only when MHVTL's own tables say the drive refuses "
"the cartridge - which it does by accepting the move and then unloading "
"the tape in the drive (usr/cmd/vtltape.c:1512), leaving it for someone to"
" unmount. An unrecognised barcode or drive is compatible and known=False."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.mount_matrix:1
#: ffd3619bc289453b8872f49e8df6b3d6 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid "{slot_num: {drive_num: verdict}} for every loaded slot and every drive."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.compatibility.mount_matrix:3
#: d89e1c63e0254564b05e66753d44fc7d of
msgid ""
"Slots and drives are the mtx status dicts, with the drive's product "
"string under 'model'. A loaded drive still gets a verdict - the page "
"shows why it is not offered separately from whether the tape would fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:281 3ffa799380144515bced8a6e59a7b896
msgid "``media``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:283 7765180f800d479ab2ada53134cbdb71
#: 7bbc4cc0c60a449fa547fd1cead6ad1f apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:1 of
msgid "The tape files on disk, under the media directory."
msgstr ""

#: 099b3c4879964189ae0c6e040e7daea9 apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:3 of
msgid ""
"Gathers tape_operations_service.py:1934 (mktape), :2060 (the rm -rf), "
":2682 (_get_tape_size_mb) and :2716 (_get_tape_used_mb)."
msgstr ""

#: 025eb354966e4fe394b568237cbcf7b1 apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:6 of
msgid ""
"Three things are different here, each for a reason found on a running "
"host."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:8 befb3fc2b720404d9efa01165ff5932e of
msgid "BOTH MEDIA LAYOUTS. mhvtl 1.7 wrote one set of files per tape:"
msgstr ""

#: 5b17bd23e4654391a398336908bc174c apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:10 of
msgid "E01001L8/data  E01001L8/indx  E01001L8/meta"
msgstr ""

#: 59ed1d472e604eb1b29971d128ec6735 apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:12 of
msgid "1.8 splits them per LTFS partition, and adds a MAM file:"
msgstr ""

#: 952559826d6e4dd887386a45d3cf3bb0 apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:14 of
msgid "E01001L8/data.0  E01001L8/indx.0  E01001L8/meta.0  E01001L8/mam"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:16 e8e0688d3daa4ee58d5fdd992e7945b9 of
msgid ""
"Code that looked for a file named exactly `data` reported every tape as 0"
" bytes after the upgrade, silently."
msgstr ""

#: 75644994654743f89267b4dde6990a0a apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:19 of
msgid ""
"CAPACITY COMES FROM THE MAM, WHICH SAYS WHAT IT HOLDS. The old reader "
"took a big-endian u64 at offset 8 of `meta` and called it the capacity. "
"In 1.8 those bytes are zeros, so it returned 0 - a tape that looks empty "
"and full at once. This module then reported the capacity as unknown "
"rather than guess, which left every unloaded tape without a size."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:25 cb951850693e402ea43b3d3b36197e54 of
msgid ""
"The MAM file is not a guess, though: mhvtl writes it as type-length-value"
" \"to keep mam auto-descriptive\" (usr/vtlcart.c:write_mam), after two "
"uint32 version fields, and the ids are the SCSI ones - 0x0000 remaining "
"capacity, 0x0001 maximum capacity, both 8-byte big-endian "
"(usr/vtllib.c:188). Reading those two is reading what the file says it "
"contains, and it answers for a tape sitting in a slot, which `vtlcmd "
"stats` cannot."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:32 b362c2a217d94134aab67a623226b688 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The drive is still the authority for a tape it holds: the MAM is written "
"back when the tape is unloaded, so mid-backup it is behind - 59.2% on "
"disk while the drive reported 75.7%."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media:36 fcb046541a0a413dad811f0e09c933cc of
msgid ""
"DELETION IS CONTAINED. The barcode is validated and the resolved path is "
"checked to be a direct child of the media directory before anything is "
"removed. The original interpolated the barcode straight into `sudo rm -rf"
" /opt/mhvtl/<barcode>`."
msgstr ""

#: 79a9342e825e468caaa9b025bebd1a27
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.DATA_FILE_RE:1 of
msgid "`data` (1.7) or `data.0`, `data.1` (1.8)."
msgstr ""

#: 7704b6eec7564784a1d6df7d4f7c928e
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.DATA_FILE_RE:3 of
msgid "Data files, either layout"
msgstr ""

#: 6cecd5f77fb74530a529709a8bd86014
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.MediaPathRefused:1 of
msgid "The barcode does not resolve to a path inside the media directory."
msgstr ""

#: 57d70a91f98343d09944e229d762d041
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.path_for:1 of
msgid "Where a tape's files live, refusing anything that escapes the directory."
msgstr ""

#: 0b26887d7349419b8263f8043c46b558
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.path_for:3 of
msgid ""
"Two checks, because this feeds `rm -rf`: the barcode must be a barcode, "
"and the resolved path must be a direct child of the media directory."
msgstr ""

#: 4831d34b99d541ed924c5a6c8ff2fc79
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.MediaUsage:1 of
msgid "What a tape's files say about it."
msgstr ""

#: 3016eb418056483cbacb15d2fd13ff3b
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.MAM_HEADER:1 of
msgid ""
"The MAM is TLV after two uint32 version fields; these are the SCSI "
"attribute ids for what a tape holds, each an 8-byte big-endian count of "
"bytes (mhvtl usr/vtllib.c:188)."
msgstr ""

#: 01a3960cd1514d1082c8131bbf0efc30
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.MAM_LIMIT:1 of
msgid "A MAM is about a kilobyte; anything far larger is not one."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.read_mam:1
#: ea4629db05da4f2c99ae01378c94d56f of
msgid "The attributes in a MAM file, by id."
msgstr ""

#: 60f1cd96136348f6bdab4a59d657d74d
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.read_mam:3 of
msgid ""
"Stops at the first record that does not fit rather than raising: a MAM "
"being rewritten as this reads it is a short or torn file, not a reason to"
" fail a page."
msgstr ""

#: 68b25b9aeeb14d1fb0c43e6229ddc622
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.capacity_from_mam:1 of
msgid "(capacity, remaining) in bytes, or (None, None) if the file cannot say."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.read_mams:1
#: bd1d63e05fb94bea8f564dc8942a67fe of
msgid ""
"Every tape's MAM file in one call, for the same reason usage_for_all "
"exists: one sudo per page, not one per tape."
msgstr ""

#: 7bfc41df963540e5bd0cb12f4b8f223c
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.read_mams:4 of
msgid ""
"Through tar, because the sudoers rules allow tar and do not allow a shell"
" - and should not: a rule for `sh -c` is a rule for anything. tar names "
"each member, so the files come back separated and identified, which `cat`"
" of several files does not manage."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.usage:1 e7d1c1e2090c468bba91069d5d7da2ee
#: of
msgid "One tape's disk usage. Prefer usage_for_all() when asking about many."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.usage_for_all:1
#: bd32ca079fdb43719446b4744c71e14c of
msgid "Disk usage for many tapes in one pass."
msgstr ""

#: 441a39bf0af94bba825ae90081eb93ba
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.usage_for_all:3 of
msgid ""
"One `find` over the media directory instead of two sudo calls per tape. "
"The old per-tape reads cost about 69ms each, so listing a 32-tape library"
" spent over four seconds shelling out - on every page load."
msgstr ""

#: aa071010e4574dcd91fb025e901b975e
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.create:1 of
msgid "Create a tape's files with mktape."
msgstr ""

#: 3c717694df8747f7a6dca9bc79f55dfe
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.create:3 of
msgid ""
"mktape writes into the library's home directory itself; base is accepted "
"so a test can point at a scratch directory."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.delete:1
#: f5b8152185ad43f895bdf61a2d14a211 of
msgid "Remove a tape's files."
msgstr ""

#: 05f98e697ea545a68183ad27db4800bf
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.delete:3 of
msgid ""
"path_for() has already refused anything that is not a plain barcode "
"resolving inside the media directory, so the path handed to rm is one "
"this module built, not one a caller supplied."
msgstr ""

#: 9494ae5fc1144f8da8eff4543bb88cdf
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.media.list_media:1 of
msgid "Every barcode with a directory on disk, whether or not a library knows it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:293 586ce0e63dce48bd88474314a5a63b41
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models:1 fd99e3cc3f3b435d9d1f678df76a5626 of
msgid "Tape dataclasses."
msgstr ""

#: 479b5fa297ce438ba0e457ae5a7ce35b apps.libraries.services.tapes.models:3 of
msgid ""
"Replaces TapeInfo from tape_operations_service.py:1897. The difference "
"worth noting is that capacity and used are optional: a tape whose size "
"cannot be read reports None rather than 0, because 0 reads as \"blank "
"tape\" and sends an operator looking for a problem that does not exist."
msgstr ""

#: aad05eeeeb4f4720a7846507c67bc973
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models.TapeInfo:1 of
msgid "One tape, as the library configuration and the disk describe it."
msgstr ""

#: 4a9f64ff059643aea0e35d8725e2687d
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models.TapeInfo.kind:1 of
msgid "data, clean or WORM."
msgstr ""

#: 0dcd736f8d2b45f2965ecc051ae673d0
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models.TapeInfo.density_class:1 of
msgid "Which generation colour the tape is drawn in."
msgstr ""

#: 1aceca03c9544a1abeba251cd2b8c9a7
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models.TapeInfo.summary:1 of
msgid ""
"What a tape has left, the way a drive is described in a file manager: "
"\"117 MB free of 480 MB\"."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models.TapeInfo.summary:4
#: b2e23352b1d14d918a1989550bc7ea19 of
msgid ""
"Worded here rather than in a template or a page script, so the library "
"page, the tape inventory and `mhvtl tape list` say the same thing about "
"the same tape."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.models.TapeInfo.fullness:1
#: b2c20d1b8db04b47a18ad4509a781030 of
msgid ""
"How alarming the bar should look. The thresholds are in core.units, "
"shared with the live drive panel: the same tape must not be described one"
" way in a slot and another in a drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:303 8009b4f2ff2c4b0889d339749bd81e51
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service:1 cd45a6a9ef94468f836a4627836149c6 of
msgid "Tape create, bulk create, delete and list."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service:3 d9eac5b2f23c457fbb84bfc1bf4d1d4b of
msgid ""
"Moved from tape_operations_service.py:1934 (create_tape), :2086 "
"(delete_tape), :2179 (list_tapes) and :2229 (create_tapes_bulk), with the"
" library_contents editing that went with them."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service:7 bd7bed2a521c4f42a758985e7b273076 of
msgid ""
"A tape is only created in a density one of the library's drives loads, "
"and with a barcode whose suffix names that density: MHVTL's drives refuse"
" other media on load, and its tools read the density back from the "
"suffix."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service:11 e3016d6c1a1249b88f53bf28ae2d6829 of
msgid ""
"The order of operations on create is deliberate: validate, check the slot"
" is free and the barcode unused, make the media, then record it in "
"library_contents. A failure after the media is made leaves a file with no"
" slot, which an operator can see and clean up; a failure the other way "
"round leaves a slot pointing at a tape that does not exist, which the "
"library reports as a read error at the worst moment."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.CONTENTS_RE:1
#: e645b9d30921447789010f6da97ad026 of
msgid "library_contents.10 -> 10, as in libraries/orphans."
msgstr ""

#: 0a23df406d7040a48e6479868164c705
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService:1 of
msgid ""
"Tapes, as library_contents records them and the media directory holds "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: 7ea1c3e49863445b9b2f96459884b9d1
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService:3 of
msgid "TapeService().list(10) TapeService().create(10, 'E01033L8', slot=33)"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.list:1
#: c72339080ac145e0b69db8075dc6cb7c of
msgid "Every tape in a library."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.list:3
#: e0249d29318b4ef0bbc6de5435aaed32 of
msgid ""
"with_usage=False skips the disk measurement entirely, for callers that "
"only need to know what is in which slot."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.next_barcode:1
#: bc642c56df58488e8b901a72e16f8391 of
msgid "The next free barcode in the series this library already uses."
msgstr ""

#: 3727380db9ba48feac1e976217e84381
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.barcode_prefix:1 of
msgid "The three-character prefix this library's tapes use."
msgstr ""

#: 55a286b1bc494c6cb41feab608562648
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.barcode_prefix:3 of
msgid ""
"What the tapes already in it use, falling back to the vendor profile's "
"leading letter and the library id - the same rule the create form "
"applies. It lived in two views, each with its own copy of the profile "
"lookup; a library's barcode series is a fact about the library, so it "
"belongs here."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.media_for_library:1
#: f17f15c747a44d40a8f5985dc5a37520 of
msgid "Which tapes this library's drives can use."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.media_for_library:3
#: cb13eb4091074998bf1f18f02326ebad of
msgid "{'drives': [product, ...], 'known': bool, 'default': density or None,"
msgstr ""

#: 93e4872d30464755b7020737a5f2f925
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.media_for_library:4 of
msgid "'media': [{'density', 'suffix', 'writable', 'writable_in',"
msgstr ""

#: 75db8f23c7034d448f58732c1fdc5f79
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.media_for_library:5 of
msgid "'read_only_in'}, ...]}"
msgstr ""

#: 1e2c822ca6934994a9c8a5709a02887a
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.media_for_library:7 of
msgid ""
"Media are in the order the drives list them, native first, so the first "
"is the natural default. known is False when device.conf cannot be read or"
" the library has no drive MHVTL gives a media list; callers then offer "
"everything and let MHVTL decide."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.check_media:1
#: c56e0009d4fb4173956eac2cba29623e of
msgid "Why a tape of this density cannot be made here, or None if it can."
msgstr ""

#: 976aa4d1379d4f289689c4c8c5cc875d
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.check_media:3 of
msgid ""
"Refuses a density mktape does not accept, a barcode whose suffix names a "
"different density, and a density none of the library's drives load. A "
"library whose drives are unknown is not refused."
msgstr ""

#: aa8d04433552411da10a5c7d85743993
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create:1 of
msgid "Create one tape and put it in a slot."
msgstr ""

#: 6b8c22435b70409a8bdbc039fcd524d8
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create:3 of
msgid ""
"The density defaults to what the barcode's suffix says, then to the "
"library's first writable medium. check_media=False skips the drive check,"
" for create_bulk, which has already made it once for the run."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create_bulk:1
#: cdeb26be8754436dbf3e7e5043efaf7f of
msgid "Create a numbered run of tapes."
msgstr ""

#: 97e98e510e5a4cf98133df582dfb7aeb
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create_bulk:3 of
msgid ""
"Stops at the first failure and reports what was made, rather than "
"carrying on and leaving the operator to work out which of fifty tapes "
"exist. A density with no suffix gets the density's suffix; a suffix with "
"no density gets the suffix's density; the pair is checked against the "
"library's drives once, before anything is made."
msgstr ""

#: ad0a62de63d745f1818dd84358397b6d
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.adopt:1 of
msgid "Put a tape that already has media files into a library's slot."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.adopt:3
#: e04f0f2d8e924377b6bb321b7ac956b9 of
msgid ""
"The counterpart of `delete` without remove_media, which leaves a tape's "
"data on disk with no library listing it (libraries/orphans reports "
"those). Nothing is written to the media: this only adds the barcode to "
"library_contents, so the tape comes back with everything that was on it."
msgstr ""

#: 9c4085e671c148bf97d7eb61e2af5fd6
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.adopt:9 of
msgid ""
"Refuses a barcode another library already lists - two libraries claiming "
"one tape means two robots moving the same data."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.unassigned:1
#: b4d28a7db17941b2b86336cef48a6392 of
msgid "Tapes whose files are on disk but that no library_contents lists."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.unassigned:3
#: e1c6694feba8436fa9f9ef539d278e05 of
msgid ""
"The inventory side of libraries/orphans: what `delete` without "
"remove_media leaves, and what a restored media directory brings back. "
"Each one can be given to a library again with adopt()."
msgstr ""

#: 208510b3c2a943edb44510c13bf92d48
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.owner_of:1 of
msgid ""
"The id of the library whose library_contents lists this barcode, or None."
" Every contents file in the configuration directory is read, not only the"
" declared libraries: a tape in a library that is merely stopped still "
"belongs to it."
msgstr ""

#: 01d2eabfa0a64da99483747f668cbe35
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create_missing:1 of
msgid ""
"Make the media files for barcodes library_contents lists but that have "
"none on disk."
msgstr ""

#: 3490ddb4e0c8424c97568680177d00c8
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create_missing:4 of
msgid ""
"What a new library needs - its library_contents is written with the "
"barcodes, the files are not - and the repair after a configuration "
"restore. Each tape's density comes from its barcode suffix, then from "
"`density`, then from the library's first writable medium. Barcodes that "
"already have files are left alone."
msgstr ""

#: 84b7788e48af4b168b561697a6b40c07
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.create_missing:10 of
msgid ""
"Moved from the adapter's create_tapes_from_library_contents, which took "
"no density; the create-library workflow passed one, so the call raised "
"TypeError and no new library got its tapes."
msgstr ""

#: 66e83b97318c4fe7999d05b7287a0a38
#: apps.libraries.services.tapes.service.TapeService.delete:1 of
msgid "Remove a tape from its slot, and optionally delete its files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:311 1519102f250c418f9550701c0ac0664f
msgid "``services.operations``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:313 0dc6944756b34d7ea5d88a5901f00d77
msgid "Moving tapes around: mtx, mt and vtlcmd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:316 a3073a5abbae4df9a7acf1184395f316
msgid "``mounting``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:318 f8197eaa33e84da39a17530ce6fb5a7a
msgid ""
"What the mount page reads: the slot map, each drive's model, and every "
"loaded cartridge's verdict for every drive."
msgstr ""

#: 599d7d89489f41f9a9d96b5aa8292e5f
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting:1 of
msgid ""
"What the mount page needs: the slot map, each drive's model, and whether "
"each loaded cartridge can go into each drive."
msgstr ""

#: 0830d3ba25ff4917adf619b05d73182e
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting:4 of
msgid ""
"Moved from the adapter's get_library_status_with_lto, "
"check_mount_compatibility and get_drives_for_library, which the operator "
"AJAX endpoints called. The compatibility answers come from "
"tapes/compatibility.verdict, which reads MHVTL's own drive media tables "
"(profiles/personalities)."
msgstr ""

#: 56327dd6c5b44bfabf964fb5689174d7
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting:9 of
msgid ""
"drive_num is the number mtx uses: the drive's `Slot:` in device.conf "
"minus one, not its position in the file."
msgstr ""

#: 79ef9db34f9a4cba8eb95c140eb5a8af
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting.library_drives:1 of
msgid "A library's drives from device.conf, ordered by drive_num."
msgstr ""

#: 0d088db263784278b90d3c4e6e3207e4
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting.mount_status:1 of
msgid ""
"The slot map with every tape's and drive's generation, and every loaded "
"slot's verdict for every drive (mount_matrix)."
msgstr ""

#: 52bbcdcd0e464185a5380640152cb51d
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting.mount_status:4 of
msgid ""
"data carries the keys the mount page reads: drives, storage_slots, "
"import_export_slots, slot_summary, compatibility_info, mount_matrix and "
"drive_info."
msgstr ""

#: 448fac381a4940c1aa83e3c67c8ef8c9
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting.mount_check:1 of
msgid "Can the tape in this slot be mounted into this drive?"
msgstr ""

#: 905ca34850e94a25893128c60b61f21c
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mounting.mount_check:3 of
msgid ""
"Checked in this order - slot exists, slot has a tape, drive exists, drive"
" is free, the drive loads the cartridge - because each answer is a "
"different thing for the operator to do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:327 ba7ba384580c4788988e0ccdad24c21b
msgid "``mt``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:329 86d0a57a4c694e6cba8388caa538729f
#: 9a647cdd0eb64ee9936e08f5b53062b7 apps.libraries.services.operations.mt:1 of
msgid "The mt wrapper - drive-level status."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt:3 ea48a6dbea6d42b8b3f1912de6c78ffd of
msgid ""
"Moved from tape_operations_service.py:985. mt talks to the tape device "
"itself (/dev/st*, or /dev/nst* to avoid rewinding on close), so it "
"answers questions mtx cannot: what density the loaded media is, whether "
"the drive is at BOT, how many soft errors it has seen."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt:8 d621fd50d32f43cbab492804945ff300 of
msgid ""
"It goes through SCSI, so it fails with \"Device or resource busy\" while "
"a backup holds the drive. When that happens the answer is vtlcmd stats, "
"not a retry."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.FLAG_RE:1
#: f87e80b0b9c14879834ae1348a0e4028 of
msgid ""
"WR_PROT, BOT, EOT, DR_OPEN, ONLINE, IM_REP_EN. Matched as whole words "
"because the same output carries the hex status value, and a substring "
"search for BOT finds it there."
msgstr ""

#: 642faf41840446a3808f6e96517662b8
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.FLAG_RE:5 of
msgid "The flag names on mt's \"General status bits\" line"
msgstr ""

#: 8a5cb77a92814580a6cc5e860fc5339f
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.DriveStatus:1 of
msgid "What mt reports about a drive."
msgstr ""

#: 7751bf34c0574cadb2c09de589d3e594
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.DriveStatus.write_protected:1 of
msgid "From the \"General status bits on\" line, which mt prints as flag names."
msgstr ""

#: 27ec700fdd1f430780668d99b2f28a13
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.DriveStatus.ready:1 of
msgid "online with the door shut."
msgstr ""

#: 81e1c3fc62084487885d647ca08e83b4
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.DriveStatus.ready:3 of
msgid "Loaded and usable"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.DriveStatus.has_medium:1
#: f2999936840a4667bfdff4582e80dbf0 of
msgid "A drive with no tape reports file/block -1."
msgstr ""

#: 4ef5a095fd0b4701b8b89842524cce24
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.non_rewinding:1 of
msgid "The node that does not rewind the tape when it is closed."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.non_rewinding:3
#: d6513194e61f4c41a02a40f9ee3b8c64 of
msgid ""
"/dev/stN rewinds on close; /dev/nstN is the same drive without that. It "
"matters for reading as much as for writing: `mt -f /dev/st0 status` "
"closes the device and therefore moves the tape, so asking a drive what it"
" is doing changes what it is doing. Two `mhvtl status drive` runs a "
"minute apart reported different positions for that reason."
msgstr ""

#: 975e4d524a4e456390980038e5e18d7d
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.non_rewinding:9 of
msgid ""
"Falls back to whatever was passed when there is no non-rewinding node - a"
" /dev/sg node, or a host that does not create them."
msgstr ""

#: 3de3e5c5ce4a461096e8ff6d785aa444
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.parse:1 of
msgid "Parse `mt status` output."
msgstr ""

#: 51dd4891191642c0acdff93cf827c81f
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.status:1 of
msgid "Read a drive's status. Not retried: a busy drive stays busy for a while."
msgstr ""

#: 6ffc8a0d4e0549a98f07425904f8182c
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mt.status:3 of
msgid "Read through the non-rewinding node, so asking does not move the tape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:337 2c191c5ada744de980bbe0210b613f30
msgid "``mtx``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:339 12dd70e9c37f43bab515e972f5e8cbbd
#: apps.libraries.services.operations.mtx:1 da8d018965f445b7bb77b4698b64db85 of
msgid "The mtx wrapper and its output parser."
msgstr ""

