"IscsiService().status() "
"IscsiService().create_target('iqn.2026-01.com.example:library10')"
msgstr ""

#: 75d337efdb2c474b8c3674adbc1425ac
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.status:1 of
msgid "Service state, targets and backstores in one answer."
msgstr ""

#: 3ff57332ae5348d9aabd59d1677b8909
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.available_devices:1 of
msgid "The MHVTL devices that can be exported."
msgstr ""

#: 23a2282c3dfa432d96a5b1828a93deb9
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.available_devices:3 of
msgid ""
"Only the generic (/dev/sg) node is usable for a pscsi backstore, so a "
"device without one is not offered. Moved from the old adapter (once "
"adapters/iscsi_service.get_available_scsi_devices)."
msgstr ""

#: 231feccbd6b446cda9bda94027cadcf8
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.save_config:1 of
msgid "Write the running configuration to saveconfig.json."
msgstr ""

#: 5869896682684c02b3ea7f5ffa4ab2ca
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.restore_config:1 of
msgid "Load the saved configuration back into the kernel."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.restore_config:3
#: cb4d9524195441c694d846a0bf25582a of
msgid ""
"A pscsi backstore names a /dev/sgN path, and those numbers change when "
"the SCSI modules reload, so a restore can bring back a target that "
"exports the wrong device; remap.py fixes that by SCSI address."
msgstr ""

#: 4902f4ffd40b4602be92e8ee77d76824
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.create_backstore:1 of
msgid "Export a device."
msgstr ""

#: 74ff4e0f71d34a44a5527a2eea27d822
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.create_backstore:3 of
msgid ""
"The device is checked against the MHVTL devices first: exporting a disk "
"that is not a virtual tape device publishes it to any initiator that "
"connects. A pscsi backstore is recorded against the daemon it bound to, "
"so a later restart of that daemon shows up as stale (see bindings.py); "
"export_library records its backstores once, at the end."
msgstr ""

#: 5659c1d98ef547c89a0df8b784a628d2
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.create_lun:1 of
msgid "Map a backstore into a target, at LUN `lun` or the next free one."
