#: 383e27aeb26241009f88388b8ab9ea0b
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.service:1 of
msgid "start, stop, restart, enable or disable target.service."
msgstr ""

#: a3dc9da620cc465aa3f4ab7e08ae6c35
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.service:3 of
msgid ""
"The action is matched against a fixed set rather than passed through to "
"systemctl: this is reachable from a web form, and `mask` or `isolate` are"
" not things a form should be able to ask for."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.set_chap:1
#: bdd175b749864aebbbd85e2e258e5cce of
msgid "Require CHAP, for one initiator's ACL or target-wide."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.set_chap:3
#: cb978add6a74403b8a89dd2dae9c2638 of
msgid ""
"With `initiator`, the credentials are that ACL's. Without it they are the"
" target's own, used by any initiator that comes in through \"Allow all "
"initiators\" - which is the only way to put a password on an open target."
" Mutual CHAP adds the target proving itself to the initiator. Either way "
"the TPG's authentication attribute is switched on, which is what makes "
"LIO refuse a login without the password."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.clear_chap:1
#: eac780f2055245ee81d0fed0dd70df13 of
msgid ""
"Remove CHAP from one ACL or from the target, and stop requiring it once "
"no credentials are left anywhere on the target."
msgstr ""

#: 6463f30d567d4da69299c245d6a7781f
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.service.IscsiService.chap_in_use:1 of
msgid "Whether any credentials are left on the target or its ACLs."
