msgstr ""

#: 099e4c5398fa42e68ff5ddc3d5a9a135
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.validate_iqn:1 of
msgid "Return the IQN, or explain why it was refused."
msgstr ""

#: 80f2fa97a68749bea9dd15c6cd91e961
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.mhvtl_devices:1 of
msgid "The device nodes MHVTL currently owns - the only ones worth exporting."
msgstr ""

#: 1e575726bdbd4ca5a98f7237d758e7b7
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.validate_device:1 of
msgid "Check a device path before it is exported to the network."
msgstr ""

#: 81e1c47974d34756a2d1407c7694bfc2
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.validate_device:3 of
msgid ""
"Two gates: it has to look like an MHVTL device node, and it has to be one"
" this host actually has. Exporting /dev/sda is a decision, not a typo, so"
" a caller that means it passes allow_any."
msgstr ""

#: 148ab31f4b9441e5a7f0d390e604a7cc
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.run:1 of
msgid "Run one targetcli command."
msgstr ""

#: 73b64699923d499fa58a62915de3a1ad
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.run:3 of
msgid ""
"An argument list, never a shell string: a backstore name arrives from a "
"form."
msgstr ""

#: 38cb9a4deac34b52809d7e2adf20960f
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.save_config:1 of
msgid "Persist the running configuration, so it survives a reboot."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.create_block_backstore:1
#: f804bd26ec5c4b3cb47d7abd393ffbfb of
msgid ""
"Export a block device. The device is validated first; see the module "
"docstring."
msgstr ""

#: 1607961ca27f499aaf1e3fe8527734cb
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.create_pscsi_backstore:1 of
msgid "Export a SCSI device pass-through - how a tape drive is exported."
msgstr ""

#: ab59a4b44dc842c887fecd94b649b8d3
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.create_lun:1 of
msgid ""
"Map a backstore into a target; targetcli picks the number unless `lun` "
"names one. A changer goes at LUN 0: some backup software stops scanning "
"at the first tape drive it meets."
msgstr ""

#: 7529a07e16fc41f4afecbdd86c8ded57
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.create_acl:1 of
msgid "Allow one initiator to see this target."
msgstr ""

#: 629ef882b2744f6481f47fd304f9558e
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.delete_portal:3 of
msgid ""
"Deleting the last portal leaves a target nothing can connect to, which "
"looks from the initiator side exactly like the target being gone."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.set_auth:1
#: c3b08b2d5a5f45349415b7199afea13e of
msgid "Set, or with empty values clear, CHAP on one ACL or on the whole TPG."
msgstr ""

#: a096bff36df34878a45a6d94eebc8bcd
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.set_auth:3 of
msgid ""
"On an ACL it applies to that initiator; on the TPG it applies to the "
"initiators that come in without an ACL of their own (generate_node_acls)."
" The values are checked unless every one is empty (clearing)."
msgstr ""

#: ab0d3d701491491382ebf837a2002099
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.targetcli.set_attribute:1 of
msgid "Set a TPG attribute, such as generate_node_acls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:534 0a85ec5998f443d3aa105c32c80940f3
#: 48564dd26e204155ac515f7b5e37f18e apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow:1 of
msgid "Exporting a whole library over iSCSI, in one step."
msgstr ""

#: 996d823f735c49a3b7e86b998c8d8bde apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow:3 of
msgid ""
"Moved from iscsi_service.py:export_library. It is a sequence, not an "
"operation: a target, then a pscsi backstore per device, then a LUN per "
"backstore, then the access rule. Any of those can fail on its own, and "
"what the operator needs to know is which - a target with three of its "
"four drives exported is a working library that will stall on the fourth."
msgstr ""

#: 0902ef7cd6b64438b9cccff88c0bd722 apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow:9 of
msgid ""
"The same shape as libraries/workflow.py, and for the same reason: this "
"lived inside a view, so there was no way to export a library except by "
"submitting the form, and no way to report the steps except as flash "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow:13 f214c847db8042c7980fa3b77331c274
#: of
msgid ""
"report = export_library(10, devices) report.ok            # every step "
"succeeded report.steps         # what happened, in order report.warnings"
"      # what did not, without stopping the rest"
msgstr ""

#: 21404a561aed42949d2426387a27b8cb apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow:18
#: of
msgid ""
"A note on LUN order. The changer is exported as LUN 0 and the drives "
"follow. Backup applications look for the medium changer at the lowest "
"LUN, and some will not scan past a tape drive to find it, so the order is"
" deliberate rather than whatever the caller happened to pass."
msgstr ""

#: 0bf51765ee694ca3a8fd2956d7da6794
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.ExportReport:1 of
msgid "What the export did, step by step."
msgstr ""

#: 8eece5b2930c4175b5fd8d7b38b24d19
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.default_iqn:1 of
msgid "iqn.<year>-<month>.com.mhvtl:library<N>."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.default_iqn:3
#: b965dab3e30441f6b0cd470cb8e88b90 of
msgid ""
"The date is the naming authority's, not today's event: RFC 3720 wants the"
" year and month at which the naming authority owned the domain. "
"Generating it from today is what MHVTL's own examples do and what every "
"target on this host already uses, so it stays."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library:1
#: c8f20609b10a4d55acd045841f01a934 of
msgid "Create a target exporting a library's changer and drives."
msgstr ""

#: 9a4b243328a5414491e8ef75a09d33d9
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library:3 of
msgid "names the target and its backstores."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library:4
#: b2cd3c492ccc40758d3982ec8e2fe0d8 of
msgid ""
"dicts with device_path, and optionally name and type. A device whose type"
" is \"changer\" is exported first, as LUN 0."
msgstr ""

#: 5ed5f81646554ec9b74a7b6609e3961d
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library:6 of
msgid "the target name; generated from the library id when not given."
msgstr ""

#: 11ae133eda284e4c940d3ce9dc4db3f4
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library:7 of
msgid ""
"sets generate_node_acls, which lets anything that connects attach. False "
"with an initiator_iqn creates an ACL for that initiator alone."
msgstr ""

#: 0fe5eb5fc0b248bf9b57a3e4550259a5
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.export_library:11 of
msgid ""
"The target is created first and is not rolled back if a later step fails:"
" an operator with a half-exported library wants to add the missing drive,"
" not to start again. What failed is in the report."
msgstr ""

#: 8b984bf1c2014632b082ed0f634c1f1d
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.OUR_BACKSTORE:1 of
msgid ""
"lib<L>_changer, lib<L>_drive<N>. The same names workflow writes above and"
" remap.py reads; anything else in the configuration was made by hand and "
"is left alone. The names this code gives a library's backstores, and the "
"only ones it will remove. One expression, used by both readers below: "
"written twice, they disagreed - the other accepted lib50_drivefoo."
msgstr ""

#: acfd8dfc9fce4d208921d7ad040c21b8
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.OUR_BACKSTORE:8 of
msgid "A backstore this library's export made"
msgstr ""

#: 6a2baf7a0b2c4a91b70e59dcd986d690
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.library_of:1 of
msgid "Which library a target exports, or None when it is not one of ours."
msgstr ""

#: 010c65ed616348fa80ac91c28bdd7017
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.library_of:3 of
msgid ""
"Read from the backstores its LUNs use - lib<L>_changer, lib<L>_drive<N> -"
" rather than from the target's name. The name is only a default: an "
"export made with --iqn says nothing about the library, while the "
"backstores are what this code wrote and what remap reads."
msgstr ""

#: 1af5338273f64dc3841aff3fb80d646c
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.library_of:8 of
msgid ""
"A target whose LUNs point at more than one library is not one library's "
"export, and answers None."
msgstr ""

#: 8d170b761d7a4d20a3db14aafca4f0c1
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.unexport_library:1 of
msgid "Stop exporting a library: its target, and the devices it exported."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.unexport_library:3
#: ef7f2fb7837b40028df30e7bbb209af9 of
msgid ""
"The inverse of export_library, and it exists because deleting the target "
"alone is not what an operator means. A target carries its LUNs and its "
"ACLs away with it; the pscsi backstores stay, holding the /dev/sg node "
"each was made with. That is right for a backstore on its own - the same "
"device can be mapped into another target - and wrong for a library that "
"is no longer exported: the next library to take that SCSI address wants "
"the node, and `iscsi remap` goes on trying to repoint a backstore at a "
"daemon that no longer exists."
msgstr ""

#: 86bf93cbb16d410e86a4fe03004569c6
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.unexport_library:12 of
msgid ""
"Only backstores this export named are removed - lib<L>_changer and "
"lib<L>_drive<N>. One made by hand with targetcli has a name we do not "
"recognise, and removing it is not ours to decide."
msgstr ""

#: 84beb808b84645af9a88dc08f0c15ec7
#: apps.libraries.services.iscsi.workflow.unexport_library:16 of
msgid ""
"remove_backstores=False deletes the target and leaves them, which is what"
" the old behaviour was; it is here for a caller that means it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:542 81fe48246b904dd09a8e5d453dd77b34
msgid "``services.verification``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:544 47f70fc1cb5d4f7da5d47c7770471fa2
msgid "Proving a library holds what is written to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:549 372991d47f064b929835e34a4158e678
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data:1 b90a922abad34bb982a23e3955ac3657
#: of
msgid "Test data: generating it, checksumming it, and checking it came back."
msgstr ""

#: 97437afd6d3d4808b762e776ece5565d apps.libraries.services.verification.data:3
#: of
msgid ""
"Moved from backup_restore_test_service.py (generate_test_data, "
"create_checksums, verify_checksums)."
msgstr ""

#: 1d496452ee1e4916a57c0b8359d8c11f apps.libraries.services.verification.data:6
#: of
msgid ""
"The data is random bytes on purpose. A tape drive with compression "
"enabled - and MHVTL configures `Compression: factor 1 enabled 1` by "
"default - will compress a file of zeros to almost nothing, so a test "
"written with zeros verifies that compression works and says nothing about"
" whether the tape holds the data. Random bytes do not compress, so the "
"number of bytes written is the number of bytes generated."
msgstr ""

#: 6b8d3fb1f3784d3fa22a8c02e1328790
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data:13 of
msgid ""
"SHA256 over the file contents, not size or mtime: tar preserves both of "
"those through a restore that has corrupted every byte in between."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.CHUNK_BYTES:1
#: b6c9682156df4fd6b6f53dd772671a1f of
msgid ""
"large enough that the syscall overhead does not dominate, small enough "
"that a 10GB test does not need 10GB of memory."
msgstr ""

#: 8572f246d83b459d873fb50495c3af90
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.CHUNK_BYTES:4 of
msgid "Read and write in 1MiB pieces"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.MANIFEST_NAME:1
#: c848bba2507147069c9697b7785ad72c of
msgid ""
"The checksum file travels with the data, so a restore can be verified "
"without the run that created it still being around."
msgstr ""

#: 59462ed212f840e0b761872851aa6142
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.generate:1 of
msgid "Write `file_count` files of random data totalling roughly size_mb."
msgstr ""

#: 0e84fb38fa6746b79d69381b756fa7ce
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.generate:3 of
msgid ""
"Roughly, because the total is divided evenly and integer division loses "
"the remainder - a 10MB test in 3 files writes 3 x 3.33MB. The exact size "
"does not matter to the verification; what matters is that it is the same "
"data coming back."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.sha256_of:1
#: efa9a8ac5a544500b28139e4e76c4853 of
msgid "The file's SHA256, read in chunks so a large tape image fits in memory."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.checksums:1
#: ddc628a344834b15970a3962cb24ef11 of
msgid "Checksum every file in a directory, and write the manifest beside them."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.checksums:3
#: b2e69db4cdbf47b384edef2457a6340e of
msgid ""
"The manifest itself is excluded, for the obvious reason that its checksum"
" cannot be inside it."
msgstr ""

#: 35ab1ce0b1424a2d88fe82685ef08f5e
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.verify:1 of
msgid "Compare restored files against the checksums taken before the write."
msgstr ""

#: abcb5dbae9314ca391fefa7c81bac123
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.data.verify:3 of
msgid ""
"Returns (verified, corrupted, missing). Missing and corrupted are kept "
"apart because they mean different things: a missing file is a tape that "
"did not hold everything, a corrupted one is a tape that held it wrongly, "
"and the second is the worse discovery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:559 00f1f11d2d5f42daba36111cb123e97c
#: 41be91c29b6f40a4b30c23b505cb0d80
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models:1 of
msgid "What a verification run reports."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models:3
#: cca7238850b6498f96f5daa8d22552ab of
msgid "Moved from backup_restore_test_service.py (TestResult, FullTestResult)."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models:5
#: d2bd23e7a90842f481aa5d10de13aba8 of
msgid ""
"A verification is a sequence of steps, and the interesting output is not "
"a boolean but which step failed and how long each took. A restore that "
"verifies in 40 seconds and one that verifies in 20 minutes are both "
"successes and only one of them means the library is usable."
msgstr ""

#: 02111376a284447e963e442b34a21d13
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models.StepResult:1 of
msgid "One step of a verification run."
msgstr ""

#: 6eb1e21f126a40509d71c3224c9c11a7
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models.VerificationReport:1 of
msgid "A whole run: every step, in order, with what it cost."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models.VerificationReport.success:1
#: bead809784a34f6994473dc9b7600084 of
msgid "Every step passed. An empty run is not a pass."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models.VerificationReport.failed_step:1
#: e2ef16001739465daf834636f0602f9b of
msgid "The first step that failed, which is the one worth reporting."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.models.VerificationReport.failed_step:3
#: eb74459462324ad88cb7b814f7d37655 of
msgid ""
"Later steps fail because this one did - a restore cannot verify data that"
" was never written - so naming them all buries the cause."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:569 73ed8a8081944fc5847feb23172384c8
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service:1
#: f20526ee2c854633bf22e6e91bdf0ad1 of
msgid "The facade: run a verification, and report it as a ServiceResult."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service:3
#: c6d15f5eadfc4651b13cd442a8bd6c3d of
msgid ""
"Everything here is thin. The steps are in workflow.py, the data handling "
"in data.py and the tape I/O in tape_io.py; this exists so a caller - a "
"view, or the CLI - has one object to hold and one result shape to read."
msgstr ""

#: 9906d4285540492db5c0bcef2811d4ff
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service.VerificationService:1 of
msgid "End-to-end proof that a library holds what is written to it."
msgstr ""

#: 6639bcb7dcb9475ca90571284d53cad8
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service.VerificationService:3 of
msgid "VerificationService().run(library_id=10, slot=1, drive_id=11)"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service.VerificationService.run:1
#: eeb520bbeb3041c58df6888eee1b2194 of
msgid "Write data to a tape, read it back, and check it is the same."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service.VerificationService.run:3
#: c086a8ed01f34aceaa150e19856a2911 of
msgid ""
"The tape in `slot` is overwritten. That is what the operation is, but it "
"is worth the caller saying so to whoever presses the button."
msgstr ""

#: 715dcc4d659249078eb90d6ebb70ea4c
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.service.VerificationService.report:1 of
msgid "The full step-by-step report, for a caller that wants every step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:577 aab6facd975c474782531c2c82701322
msgid "``tape_io``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:579 73a4a92ea48e4cea899f8b8cb861e19e
#: a403b53256e44e7eb6d87e190db6d403
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io:1 of
msgid "Writing an archive to a tape device and reading it back."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io:3
#: f2c742e497bf4f168a1e9165e019ee85 of
msgid ""
"Moved from backup_restore_test_service.py (the tar and mt parts of "
"backup_to_tape and restore_from_tape)."
msgstr ""

#: 611fdf43f7644a5fafb811b0ef8aed68
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io:6 of
msgid ""
"Three things about tape devices that the code has to get right, and which"
" are why this is its own module rather than two subprocess calls inside a"
" workflow:"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io:9
#: f809dbb2b8ec40d0a51be139662bbeb5 of
msgid ""
"/dev/stN rewinds on close and /dev/nstN does not. Writing through the "
"rewinding node and then reading through it works by accident, because the"
" rewind that happens on close is the one the read needed anyway. Writing "
"two archives that way silently overwrites the first. The non-rewinding "
"node is used where it exists, and the rewind is explicit."
msgstr ""

#: 723e470473324f0ea2ca5af173084ff3
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io:15 of
msgid ""
"A rewind is not optional before reading. A tape left at end-of-data reads"
" as an empty archive, and tar reports that as \"This does not look like a"
" tar archive\" - which reads like corruption and is really just position."
msgstr ""

#: 0b4af9ad00214f49ac853f7c1232a872
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io:19 of
msgid ""
"tar writing to a tape writes as root, so the restored files are root-"
"owned and the checksum step cannot read them. Ownership is handed back "
"after the extract."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.ARCHIVE_TIMEOUT:1
#: b73a3981f933420393418503a852e1b5 of
msgid ""
"tar to a tape is slow and the caller is a web request; ten minutes is "
"long enough for the sizes this harness generates and short enough that a "
"wedged drive does not hold a worker for ever."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.writable_device:1
#: e430f3f691134f7d9dd8fcb33de3b1ee of
msgid "The node to write through: the non-rewinding one where it exists."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.writable_device:3
#: d4a37836d99944899550b8ce73a9ebca of
msgid ""
"One rule, in operations/mt: /dev/st0 rewinds when it is closed, so a "
"second archive written to it lands on top of the first. Kept as a name "
"here because \"writable device\" is what this module means by it, and "
"because the reason differs - for a write it is about overwriting, for a "
"status read it is about not moving the tape while asking where it is."
msgstr ""

#: 7693be1678c44155bcbdf1dc05f71022
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.rewind:1 of
msgid "Wind back to the start. A warning, not an error, if it fails."
msgstr ""

#: 4da7e99ffa964626b33cad6491e8f28f
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.rewind:3 of
msgid ""
"A drive with no tape loaded refuses, and so does one that is already "
"there on some firmware; neither means the operation that follows cannot "
"run."
msgstr ""

#: 8790c057a73a4baf8125a353bfdf31ce
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.write_archive:1 of
msgid "tar the source directory onto the tape, from its parent."
msgstr ""

#: 2bdb01208b244018a2e74340eea85f84
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.write_archive:3 of
msgid ""
"From the parent so the archive contains `source/...` rather than absolute"
" paths: tar refuses to extract an absolute path without --absolute-names,"
" and an archive that will not extract is not a verified backup."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.read_archive:1
#: c213d3a9534441489df5628e4d2441f7 of
msgid "Extract the tape's archive into target, then hand back ownership."
msgstr ""

#: 881ce88f2a514f9dae45a295422ff66c
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.read_archive:3 of
msgid ""
"The rewind matters: a tape sitting at end-of-data extracts nothing, and "
"tar reports that as a malformed archive rather than an empty one."
msgstr ""

#: 72548beb2b094bbca0d0b9ba1db05542
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.extracted_root:1 of
msgid "Where the files actually landed."
msgstr ""

#: 273eb318800c4307b58aa9e44cff47e4
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.tape_io.extracted_root:3 of
msgid ""
"write_archive stores the source directory by name, so an extract into "
"`restore/` produces `restore/source/`. Returning the wrapper would make "
"every file look missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:589 02296c04b1854923a7f0c6c27542de4a
#: 912e5b0cfdbe44aab597b807d1b2f93c
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:1 of
msgid "End-to-end verification: does this library actually hold data?"
msgstr ""

#: 3d92046a89ef459db49541198bcd30d7
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:3 of
msgid "Moved from backup_restore_test_service.py:run_full_test."
msgstr ""

#: a539a8c76d8141648ffe18c5a7898d5c
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:5 of
msgid "Nine steps, and the order is the whole point:"
msgstr ""

#: 74af215a6f8343aa88857a1e29897d1f
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:7 of
msgid "generate random data            data.generate"
msgstr ""

#: 0f8305fae6004f9b8a4104d6686ccf4d
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:8 of
msgid "checksum it                     data.checksums"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:9
#: f4f31a118efc4c0b96117dc27557f8a1 of
msgid "mount the tape                  operations"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:10
#: f9ace8066c634102b3c8c3a3a8ff7bda of
msgid "write an archive to it          tape_io.write_archive"
msgstr ""

#: 49e2814eae9a423f9469994a9bd4fc83
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:11 of
msgid "unmount it                      operations"
msgstr ""

#: a5965b6faebf4acb9b86f8dbb1e9026a
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:12 of
msgid "mount it again                  operations"
msgstr ""

#: 097ae67171f34eb4ad829125e95cd042
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:13 of
msgid "read the archive back           tape_io.read_archive"
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:14
#: ce75de5a5ed84475bb03ed4c92022b4b of
msgid "checksum what came back         data.verify"
msgstr ""

#: 14d7c65ad4524e789c989e85aefeeebd
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:15 of
msgid "put the tape back in its slot   operations"
msgstr ""

#: 7de4f70cd24e453786f92fa5cef218c2
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:17 of
msgid ""
"Steps 5 and 6 are why this is a verification and not a file copy. "
"Unmounting forces the drive to flush and the robot to put the cartridge "
"away; mounting it again makes the read come off the medium rather than "
"out of a buffer that still holds what was just written. A test without "
"them passes on a drive that is writing to nothing."
msgstr ""

#: 9e21237ac4584e509817c688ce89d8ab
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:23 of
msgid ""
"The run stops at the first failing step. Later steps fail because that "
"one did - a restore cannot verify data that was never written - so "
"continuing only buries the cause under consequences."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow:27
#: b8bcb72145634d2ba7663947a2cbe905 of
msgid ""
"Step 9 runs whatever happened before it: a verification must leave the "
"library as it found it. Without it the tape stayed in the drive, and the "
"library could not then be deleted (\"1 drive(s) still have tapes "
"loaded\") until someone unmounted it by hand."
msgstr ""

#: 2c25caabf0a9475f95cb761cb1ef8a2f
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:1 of
msgid "Write data to a tape, read it back and check it is the same."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:3
#: dfbb5a92ce684307bc99152f85b733bd of
msgid "the device.conf library id."
msgstr ""

#: 810ce92ad74c46628f092706f2a37b20
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:4 of
msgid "the slot holding the tape to test. Its contents are overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:5
#: b1c05e9f36504683a7ef9683b4ddb03b of
msgid ""
"the device.conf drive id - 11, not 0. The mtx drive number is derived "
"from it, because mtx numbers drives from 0 within a library and "
"device.conf numbers them globally."
msgstr ""

#: 2969c9d145dc4f188ccf1d0f6baed709
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:8
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:9
#: c96a7903550c4f1a9483853e2cd01b10 of
msgid "how much data to write."
msgstr ""

#: 9bfe92ddea8b48e39777d1cb4ed356bd
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:10 of
msgid ""
"remove the working directory afterwards. A failed run always keeps it, "
"because the restored files are the evidence."
msgstr ""

#: 1fdf7a4901d24e54bfb3137ebc428ccc
#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.run:12 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{'changer': node, 'drive': node} to run the whole test through other "
"nodes - the library's iSCSI export, attached on this host - instead of "
"the ones device.conf maps. The tape moves, the write and the read then "
"all cross the iSCSI path."
msgstr ""

#: apps.libraries.services.verification.workflow.cleanup:1
#: fb093abcf36140f68579a1047018fe9f of
msgid "Remove a run's working directory. Kept after a failure, as evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:597 5933ebf7eb81471ba603092895a3cc16
msgid "``services.dashboard``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:599 6cae76c4d9e04f2fa7333380c3f90146
msgid "Aggregated overview data for the dashboards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../services.rst:604 9bed38a2f28147fc86447804e7642550
#: apps.libraries.services.dashboard.service:1 c683fa3ba3f24e91b5bd9327242e8471
#: of
msgid "Overview data for the dashboard tiles."
msgstr ""

#: 19daebd9fcb54a65b137c9746fbcff40 apps.libraries.services.dashboard.service:3
#: of
msgid ""
"Moved from services/dashboard_service.py, unchanged: it was written "
"during this refactor and is already in the target shape."
msgstr ""

#: 1c060ff52c054692b637f0cae43535cf apps.libraries.services.dashboard.service:6
#: of
msgid ""
"Its _section() helper is the failure-isolation pattern the rest of the "
"layer adopted - each collector runs separately, a failure is reported "
"rather than raised, and one wedged systemctl degrades one tile instead of"
" blanking the page."
msgstr ""

#: 599f1385c86840b29e35dbc1b2f911e2
#: apps.libraries.services.dashboard.service.Section:1 of
msgid "One part of the summary, which may have failed on its own."
msgstr ""

#: 5801a534c0ff47d0ad8f0528d06a3ed9
